===Etymology===
From {{inh|gmw-cfr|goh|zehan}}, from {{inh|gmw-cfr|gem-pro|*tehun|t=ten}}, from {{inh|gmw-cfr|ine-pro|*déḱm̥|t=ten}}. The vocalic development is comparable to that in {{m|gmw-cfr|sehn||to see}}, i.e. Old High German ''-eha-'' was contracted and merged with ''-ia-'' (see the same in {{cog|nl|tien}}, {{m|nl|zien}}).

